1. Objective

The Bug Submission Module provides an interface through which developers can submit software bug information to the Intelligent Bug Diagnosis Platform.

The module supports both direct text input and file upload for bug descriptions, stack traces, and error logs.

The submitted information is validated, processed, and stored so that it can be used by the subsequent bug diagnosis pipeline.

 2. Main Features

The Bug Submission Module provides the following features:

- Bug title submission
- Bug description submission
- Stack trace submission
- Error log submission
- Bug report file upload
- Log file upload
- File type validation
- Input validation
- Submission status
- Storage of submitted bug information

 3. Supported Input Methods

3.1 Direct Text Input

The developer can directly enter information into the submission interface.

The following fields are supported:

- Bug Title
- Bug Description
- Stack Trace
- Error Logs
- Affected Component
3.2 File Upload

The developer can upload bug reports and log files.

The initial prototype supports:

- `.txt`
- `.log`
- `.json`
- `.csv`

The uploaded files are validated before being processed.


