6. Input Validation

The system validates the submitted information before storing it.

Validation includes:

Checking whether required fields are provided.
Validating uploaded file types.
Checking whether uploaded files are readable.
Handling empty submissions.
Checking file size limits.
Sanitizing input data.
Validating structured JSON files.
Detecting invalid or unsupported formats.

The validation process prevents incomplete or invalid data from entering the diagnosis pipeline.

7. Required and Optional Fields
Field	Required	Description
Bug Title	Yes	Short description of the bug
Bug Description	Yes	Detailed description of the problem
Stack Trace	No	Stack trace associated with the failure
Error Logs	No	Error or application logs
Affected Component	No	Component affected by the defect
File Upload	No	Bug report or log file

At least a bug title and bug description should be provided for a valid submission.

