Structured data creation.
Storage preparation.
10. Proposed Backend API

The initial backend API is planned using Python FastAPI.

Bug Submission Endpoint
POST /api/bugs

The endpoint receives the submitted bug information and returns the submission status.

File Upload Endpoint
POST /api/bugs/upload

The endpoint handles uploaded bug reports and log files.

Get Submission Endpoint
GET /api/bugs/{submission_id}

The endpoint retrieves a previously submitted bug report.

11. Example Submission Request

A structured bug submission can contain:

{
  "title": "Application crashes while opening profile",
  "description": "The application crashes when the user opens the profile page.",
  "stack_trace": "NullPointerException at ProfileService.java:45",
  "error_logs": "ERROR ProfileService - Null reference encountered",
  "component": "Profile Service"
}
12. Example Submission Response

After successful submission, the backend can return:

{
  "submission_id": "BUG-0001",
  "status": "Submitted",
  "message": "Bug report submitted successfully."
}
13. Storage

The submitted bug reports are stored using the bug report schema defined in the M1.2 data model.

The initial prototype proposes SQLite as the submission database.

Stored information includes:

Submission ID
Bug title
Bug description
Stack trace
Error logs
Component
Uploaded file information
Processing status
Submission timestamp
14. Error Handling

The Bug Submission Module handles common submission errors.

Empty Submission
Error: Bug title and description are required.
Unsupported File
Error: Unsupported file format.
Invalid File
Error: Unable to read the uploaded file.
Large File
Error: Uploaded file exceeds the permitted size.

The system should provide clear messages so that the developer can correct the submission.

15. Security Considerations

The submission module should apply basic security controls when processing user input and uploaded files.

These include:

File type validation
File size restrictions
Input sanitization
Safe file handling
Avoiding execution of uploaded files
Protection against malicious input
Secure handling of API requests

Uploaded files are treated as data and are not executed by the system.

