18. Milestone 1 Scope

The Bug Submission Module in Milestone 1 focuses on:

Creating the submission interface.
Supporting direct bug report input.
Supporting stack trace input.
Supporting error log input.
Supporting file uploads.
Validating submitted information.
Processing submitted information.
Storing submitted bug reports.

Advanced automated diagnosis and fix recommendation capabilities will be integrated with this module in subsequent milestones.

19. Expected Outcome

At the completion of M1.3, the platform will provide a functional foundation for receiving software defect information.

Developers will be able to submit bug descriptions, stack traces, error logs, and supported bug report files. The submitted information will be validated, structured, and stored for further processing by the AI-powered diagnosis pipeline.

20. Conclusion

The Bug Submission Module provides the entry point for the Intelligent Bug Diagnosis Platform.

It enables developers to submit software defects in both text and file formats. Through validation, processing, and storage, the module prepares reliable bug information for historical defect retrieval, AI-agent analysis, root cause identification, and fix recommendation in subsequent stages of the project.
